musl libc support for vendored go-nvml dl wrapper (Saphira port).

musl's dlfcn.h lacks RTLD_DEEPBIND and RTLD_DI_ORIGIN, and musl's
dlinfo(3) rejects the ORIGIN request at runtime. Both affected symbols
are dead surface in this tree: the RTLD_DEEPBIND Go const is consumed
nowhere, and DynamicLibrary.Path() (the sole dlinfo caller) is called
nowhere in the toolkit or go-nvml. So:

- RTLD_DEEPBIND defaults to 0 (drops deepbind symbol ordering for the
  self-contained NVML library; no live path changes behavior).
- RTLD_DI_ORIGIN defaults to 6 (glibc's value): Path() compiles and
  links, and fails with a clean dlinfo error IF ever called — never
  silently wrong.
- Drop this patch when upstream go-nvml gains musl support.

diff -Naur a/vendor/github.com/NVIDIA/go-nvml/pkg/dl/dl_linux.go b/vendor/github.com/NVIDIA/go-nvml/pkg/dl/dl_linux.go
